  24:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** overflow/underflow and correct location of the stack pointer will be sense. Multiple stack configur
  25:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** considered too.
  26:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  27:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  28:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** <b>Functional Safety Stack Supervision Component - Top-Level Design</b>
  29:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  30:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  31:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \li<b>Package Model </b>\n
  32:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \image html Package_Stack.jpg
ARM GAS  C:\Users\SX2605~1.HOD\AppData\Local\Temp\ccIYNlI0.s 			page 2


  33:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  34:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  35:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** The fsStack package provides the parts outlined in the model. By compilation switch, the Stack task
  36:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** either in the usual operating mode or in test harness mode. When running in the usual operating mod
  37:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** harness part will not be linked to the package. When running in test harness mode, stub services ar
  38:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** the real stack area is separated from being manipulated and only the test server will be able to ch
  39:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  40:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  41:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** By the test harness part, it is possible to test all functions inside the stack task handler fully 
  42:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** other parts of the whole system. This is an important issue, otherwise there is a potential risk of
  43:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** which is not wanted while test.
  44:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  45:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  46:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  47:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \li<b>State Model </b>\n
  48:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \image html StateModel_Stack.jpg
  49:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  50:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  51:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** Before checking the stack, it must be initialised correctly. This happens only once and when the ge
  52:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** stack task handler the first time. After this initialisation, the stack task handler transitions in
  53:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** "FSF_STACK_READY", which will never be left during the life cycle of the whole system. In state "FS
  54:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** the stack gets checked on every call of the stack task handler.
  55:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  56:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  57:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** None
  58:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  59:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  60:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  61:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \li<b>Scenario: Stack Supervision </b>\n
  62:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \image html SequenceChart_StackSupervision.jpg
  63:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  64:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  65:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** There is not that much to explain on this scenario, except that it make use of the generic's pre-co
  66:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
  67:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  68:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** None
  69:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** \n
