 331:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** /** The Stack Channel Task.
 332:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** <pre>
 333:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 334:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****    This stack channel requires local variables to be placed on the hardware
 335:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****    stack. For the time being, the so called "compiled stack" is not supported
 336:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 337:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** </pre>
 338:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     The stack channel make use of the pre-condtion mechanism provided by the FSCOM generic. When
 339:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     scheduled, it first reports ongoing. This is in order to notify that this channel is keeping
 340:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     alive. By FSCOM, its precondition get checks. If this check fails, the channel gets moved
 341:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     into error implicitely. Succes is notified to FSCOM otherwise. Special care has to be taken
 342:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     when interpreting the mechanism:\n
 343:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     while processing of interrupts, they might be nested, even if this is not wanted currently.
 344:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     Due to this fact, some hidden stack overflow/underflow conditions may occur, and, when
 345:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     control is returned back to FSCOM, the stack pointer may point to correct position again.
 346:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     For that reason, the stack channel continuousely checks both, the location and the magics.
 347:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** 
 348:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     \return uint8_t   state of stack channel task
 349:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** 
 350:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     \pre    None
 351:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c ****     \post   Conditions for the stack are fulfilled
 352:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** */
 353:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** uint8_t FSF_ucStackHandleTask(void)
 354:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsStack.c **** {
